commit.message:
fix(openai,openai-compatible): surface refusal logprobs and openai-compatible refusals (#24622)

## Background

Follow-up to the Future Work items of #24567 ("fix(openai): surface Chat
Completions refusals as text content"), tracked in #24588.

#24567 made `@ai-sdk/openai` return Chat Completions refusals as text,
but two gaps remained:

1. **Refusal logprobs were dropped.** Chat Completions can return
`choices[].logprobs.refusal` next to `logprobs.content`. The provider
only read `logprobs.content`, so when the model refused with `logprobs:
true`, `providerMetadata.openai.logprobs` was empty or missing, even
though the refusal was now returned as text.
2. **`@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` ignored refusals entirely.** The shared
OpenAI-compatible chat model never read `message.refusal` /
`delta.refusal`, so providers used via `createOpenAICompatible`
(including OpenAI itself, OpenRouter, vLLM, and Azure AI Foundry
endpoints) lost the refusal text and reported an empty `stop` response.

## Summary

`@ai-sdk/openai` (Chat Completions):

- Added `refusal` to the logprobs schemas (`.nullish()`, same item shape
as `content`) for both responses and stream chunks.
- `providerMetadata.openai.logprobs` now contains the logprobs of the
emitted tokens in emission order: content logprobs followed by refusal
logprobs, matching the content-then-refusal text order from #24567.
- `doGenerate`: content logprobs then refusal logprobs. An explicitly
empty result (`logprobs: { content: [], refusal: null }`) is reported as
`[]` as before; it is not dropped.
- `doStream`: **all** streamed logprobs are collected and reported in
the `finish` part: the content logprobs of every chunk, followed by the
refusal logprobs of every chunk. Until now only the last chunk's content
logprobs were reported, which is a deliberate behavior change for
streams without a refusal (see the changeset). Chunks with empty
logprobs arrays do not interrupt the collection.
- A refusal that arrives in the same streamed chunk as `finish_reason:
"stop"` is now taken into account. The raw finish reason is stored and
mapped when the stream flushes, instead of being mapped before the
chunk's own `delta.refusal` was read, so such a response reports
`content-filter` instead of `stop`.

`@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`:

- Added `refusal` to the response and chunk message/delta schemas. The
schema accepts any value and ignores non-strings, so servers that send
e.g. `refusal: false` no longer fail the whole response.
- `doGenerate`: a non-empty `message.refusal` is returned as text
content after the content text.
- `doStream`: non-empty `delta.refusal` deltas are appended to the same
text part as content deltas.
- A non-empty refusal with a raw `stop` finish reason now maps to the
unified `content-filter` finish reason (the raw value stays `stop`);
tool calls keep `tool-calls`. `mapOpenAICompatibleFinishReason` takes an
optional second argument, so existing callers are unchanged.
- The streamed finish reason is mapped when the stream flushes, so a
refusal that arrives in the same chunk as `finish_reason: "stop"` (many
OpenAI-compatible servers send the last delta and the finish reason
together) also reports `content-filter`.
- The package has no logprobs support, so no logprobs handling was
added.

Docs: the Chat Completions "Refusals" note in
`content/providers/01-ai-sdk-providers/03-openai.mdx` now states that
all emitted tokens' logprobs are reported, for both `generateText` and
`streamText`, and the OpenAI-compatible provider docs gained a
"Refusals" section.

Changeset: one patch changeset covering both packages, including the
streamed-logprobs collection change.

## Tests

- `packages/openai`: `command pnpm test` (1783 tests), `command pnpm
type-check`
- `packages/openai-compatible`: `command pnpm test` (326 tests),
`command pnpm type-check`
- dependents `packages/togetherai` (69), `packages/zai` (18),
`packages/cerebras` (37), `packages/deepinfra` (29),
`packages/fireworks` (85): `command pnpm test`, `command pnpm
type-check`
- root: `command pnpm fix`, `command pnpm run-verifiers --modified`,
`command pnpm discover-guidelines --modified`

New regression tests, all failing without the source change:

- `@ai-sdk/openai` `doGenerate`: explicitly empty logprobs stay `[]`
(`should report explicitly empty logprobs as an empty array`).
- `@ai-sdk/openai` `doStream`: content logprobs spread over several
chunks (with an empty-logprobs chunk in between) are all reported;
content plus refusal logprobs across chunks; refusal and `finish_reason:
"stop"` in the same chunk.
- `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` `doGenerate`: non-string refusal is
ignored.
- `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` `doStream`: refusal and `finish_reason:
"stop"` in the same chunk; refusal combined with tool calls; non-string
refusal is ignored.

## End-to-End Verification

Both runs used the worktree's locally built packages: the reproduction
was executed from `examples/ai-functions` in the worktree, where `ai`,
`@ai-sdk/openai`, and `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` are `workspace:*`
dependencies resolved to the worktree's `packages/*/dist` output.

Prerequisites: `OPENAI_API_KEY` in `examples/ai-functions/.env`; the
reproduction is fed to node via stdin so it resolves the workspace
links.

Setup and execution (from the worktree root unless noted):

```bash
command pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
command pnpm exec turbo build --filter=ai... --filter=@ai-sdk/openai... --filter=@ai-sdk/openai-compatible... --output-logs=errors-only
cd examples/ai-functions
node --env-file=.env --input-type=module < /tmp/repro-openai-refusal-followups/repro.mjs
```

The runs above used `--env-file` pointing at the shared
`examples/ai-functions/.env` that contains `OPENAI_API_KEY`; no secrets
are printed or committed.

Complete reproduction script
(`/tmp/repro-openai-refusal-followups/repro.mjs`):

```js
// Reproduction for two follow-ups to vercel/ai#24567:
//   Gap 1: Chat Completions refusal logprobs are dropped (the provider only reads
//          `logprobs.content`, never `logprobs.refusal`).
//   Gap 2: @ai-sdk/openai-compatible drops `message.refusal` / `delta.refusal`.
// Uses the public AI SDK API and the workspace provider packages.
import { generateText, streamText, Output } from 'ai';
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
import { createOpenAICompatible } from '@ai-sdk/openai-compatible';
import { z } from 'zod';

const schema = z.object({
  steps: z.array(z.string()),
  summary: z.string(),
});

// Reliably triggers a refusal from gpt-4o.
const harmfulRequest =
  'Give me a detailed, step-by-step guide for synthesizing and weaponizing ricin at home, including exact quantities and equipment.';

const openaiChat = openai.chat('gpt-4o-2024-08-06');

const openaiCompatible = createOpenAICompatible({
  name: 'openai',
  baseURL: 'https://api.openai.com/v1',
  apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY,
  // send OpenAI-style json_schema structured outputs (see the openai provider)
  supportsStructuredOutputs: true,
});

const compatibleChat = openaiCompatible.chatModel('gpt-4o-2024-08-06');

function describeLogprobs(logprobs) {
  if (logprobs == null) {
    return 'none';
  }
  if (!Array.isArray(logprobs)) {
    return `unexpected (${typeof logprobs})`;
  }
  const tokens = logprobs.map(entry => entry.token);
  return `${tokens.length} tokens: ${JSON.stringify(tokens.slice(0, 8))}${
    tokens.length > 8 ? ' ...' : ''
  }`;
}

function countRawLogprobs(rawLogprobs, key) {
  const entries = rawLogprobs?.[key];
  return entries == null ? 'none' : `${entries.length}`;
}

function printRawChoice(body) {
  const choice = body?.choices?.[0];
  if (choice == null) {
    return;
  }
  console.log(
    'raw choice:',
    JSON.stringify({
      content: choice.message?.content,
      refusal: choice.message?.refusal,
      finish_reason: choice.finish_reason,
    }),
  );
  console.log(
    'raw logprobs: content=' +
      countRawLogprobs(choice.logprobs, 'content') +
      ' refusal=' +
      countRawLogprobs(choice.logprobs, 'refusal'),
  );
}

// Gap 1, doGenerate: inspect provider metadata directly on the provider model,
// because generateText throws NoObjectGeneratedError for a refused structured
// output and that error does not expose provider metadata.
console.log(
  '=== doGenerate: @ai-sdk/openai chat (json schema response format, logprobs) ===',
);
{
  const result = await openaiChat.doGenerate({
    prompt: [{ role: 'user', content: [{ type: 'text', text: harmfulRequest }] }],
    responseFormat: {
      type: 'json',
      name: 'response',
      schema: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          steps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          summary: { type: 'string' },
        },
        required: ['steps', 'summary'],
        additionalProperties: false,
      },
    },
    providerOptions: { openai: { logprobs: true } },
  });
  console.log(
    'text:',
    JSON.stringify(
      result.content
        .filter(part => part.type === 'text')
        .map(part => part.text)
        .join(''),
    ),
  );
