Verification notes and limits:

- Provider flow exercised: live OpenAI `chat/completions` with
`gpt-4o-2024-08-06`, once through `@ai-sdk/openai` `openai.chat()` and
once through `createOpenAICompatible` pointed at
`https://api.openai.com/v1`.
- Refusals are stochastic; a request that reliably triggers a refusal
with `gpt-4o-2024-08-06` was used. The refusal wording differs between
runs, but the raw responses confirm `logprobs.refusal` tokens and
`message.refusal` / `delta.refusal` were present in every run.
- `generateText` with structured output throws `NoObjectGeneratedError`,
which does not expose provider metadata. The `doGenerate` section of the
reproduction therefore calls the provider model directly to show
`providerMetadata.openai.logprobs` for the same request.
- Refusal logprobs are only returned by the API for structured-output
requests; a plain-text refusal arrives as `content` and was already
reported.
- `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` does not support logprobs, so gap 1 was
only verified for `@ai-sdk/openai`.
- The same-chunk finish reason ordering and the tolerance for non-string
refusals depend on server behavior that the live OpenAI API does not
exhibit (it sends the finish reason in a separate final chunk); they are
covered by the unit tests listed above.

